# Caddy in front of headnode (D-07). Replace the name with yours, and point its
# DNS record at this machine: Caddy then gets and renews the HTTPS certificate by
# itself. WebSockets (terminal, files, tunnels, agents) pass through untouched.
#
# Caddy adds X-Forwarded-For and X-Forwarded-Proto, which headnode believes only
# when the request comes from this same machine (protocol.md §1).
headnode.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080

	header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
}
